# Launch Services defaults that duti cannot set (it fails with error -50 on an
# abstract type such as public.data or a dyn.* extension type). handlers.sh writes
# these straight into LSHandlers (com.apple.launchservices.secure) with
# `defaults write ... -array-add`, through lib/ls-handlers.py. macconfig-check.sh
# reads them back. Nothing here is written by `macconfig --fix`.
# Format (pipe-delimited): kind | key | app | bundle-id
#   kind: uti  key is a UTI (role all, editor and viewer)
#         ext  key is a bare filename extension (no dot)
#
# public.data is the "unknown file" type: .env, .gitignore, .gitattributes,
# .gitconfig, .editorconfig, .npmrc, .nvmrc, .tool-versions, .prettierrc, .zshrc,
# .bashrc, .profile, Dockerfile and Brewfile all resolve to it. Files with a known
# type (source code, images, PDFs, Office) keep their own handler.
uti|public.data|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
uti|public.plain-text|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
uti|public.make-source|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
# .env.* variants have an extension of their own, which macOS gives a dyn.* type.
ext|local|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
ext|example|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
ext|production|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
ext|development|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
ext|staging|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
ext|test|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
ext|sample|CotEditor|com.coteditor.CotEditor
